      "commit": null,
      "result": "{\"exit_code\":0,\"stdout\":\"Usage: oled accounts [options] [command]\\n\\nManage the chart of accounts\\n\\nOptions:\\n  --json                 Emit NDJSON (machine-readable) instead of human output\\n  --no-color             Disable ANSI color output\\n  --config <path>        Config file to use (default ~/.oled/config.json)\\n  -h, --help             display help for command\\n\\nCommands:\\n  list [options]         List accounts\\n  tree [options]         Show accounts as a tree\\n  show [options] <id>    Show an account's details\\n  create [options]       Create a new account (single via flags, or batch via\\n                         --input)\\n  merge [options]        Merge one account into another\\n  delete [options] <id>  Delete an account\\n  adjust [options] <id>  Adjust an account balance\\n  match [options]        Match accounts against a query\\n  update [options] <id>  Update an account's name and/or metadata\\n  help [command]         display help for command\\n\\nBehavior: manages the chart of accounts. Ids are <currency>:<type>:<path> — the currency comes first and every id needs it: thb:asset:bank:kbank, usd:expense:food. Types are asset, liability, income, expense, equity; thb:asset is a ledger's type root.\\nTypical flow: match to reuse an existing account before create; read balances with tree or show.\\nOne ledger per currency: an account's currency is its id prefix, and a transaction's two accounts must share it. A USD balance lives under usd:, never under thb:.\\nExample: oled accounts match --query groceries --json\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"
